# Git: Checkpoint makes the whole working tree a diff base; the Git tab lists what changed since, Accept File moves the checkpoint for one file, Restore File puts a file back, Accept All takes a fresh checkpoint, Set Diff Base switches back to HEAD.
requires git
size 120x32
sh git init -q && printf 'def main():\n    print("hi")\n' > app.py && printf 'old notes\n' > old.txt && git add . && git commit -qm base && printf 'draft\n' > draft.txt
run
wait qed dev
snap welcome A repo with app.py and old.txt committed and draft.txt untracked.
key ctrl+p
type Git: Checkpoint
key enter
wait checkpoint
snap checkpoint Git: Checkpoint snapshots the tree, untracked draft.txt included, and the status bar shows the checkpoint as the diff base.
sh printf 'def main():\n    print("hello")\n' > app.py && printf 'brand new\n' > new.txt && rm old.txt
key alt+g
wait new.txt
snap changes After editing app.py, creating new.txt and deleting old.txt, the Git tab lists exactly those three against the checkpoint; draft.txt is not listed.
key down
wait brand new
key ctrl+p
type Accept File
key enter
wait Accepted new.txt
wait-gone brand new
snap accept-file Accept File on new.txt moves the checkpoint forward for it, so it drops off the list.
key up
wait print("hello")
key ctrl+p
type Restore File
key enter
wait Restore app.py to checkpoint?
snap restore-confirm Restore File on app.py asks first.
key down
key enter
wait Restored app.py
wait-gone print("hello")
snap restore-file Confirming puts app.py back as it was at the checkpoint, so only old.txt is left.
key ctrl+p
type Accept All
key enter
wait No changes
snap accept-all Accept All takes a fresh checkpoint: nothing is listed.
key alt+f
wait draft.txt
key enter
wait print("hi")
key ctrl+p
type Set Diff Base
key enter
wait Merge base
snap picker From app.py, Set Diff Base lists the checkpoint next to HEAD.
key enter
wait Diff base: HEAD
key alt+g
wait draft.txt
snap head Picking HEAD switches back: the Git tab lists draft.txt and new.txt as added and old.txt as deleted against HEAD.
